{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":82950,"duration_api_ms":82912,"num_turns":12,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d1277b4a-d7d9-40b0-a576-827ffac233c3","total_cost_usd":0.49093875,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40023,"cache_read_input_tokens":340090,"output_tokens":2828,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40023,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2828,"cacheReadInputTokens":340090,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40023,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.49093875,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed two amendments against the actual codebase. The first (UI label inconsistency) identifies a real UX gap where the scenario screen shows gross volume as \"Filled volume\" while all chemistry uses net water volume. The second (doc comment for LEGACY constant) is based on an incorrect factual premise — the default substrate depth is 3.0 cm, yielding 19L net volume, not 20L as the amendment claims. Adding a doc comment with the wrong derivation would be actively misleading.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-7-801f49b2","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: main.rs:597 calls geometry.water_volume_l() (gross = 22L for default) while all chemistry uses state.water_volume_l() (net = 19L with default 3cm substrate). This is a genuine inconsistency — users who back-calculate concentrations from the displayed 'Filled volume' will get wrong answers. Either relabeling as 'Tank capacity' or showing both gross and net volumes would resolve the discrepancy cheaply."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-501d15bd","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's factual premise is wrong. It claims LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L=20.0 derives from '40×25×22/1000 − 40×25×2/1000 = 20L', assuming a 2cm default substrate depth. But the actual default SubstrateLayerState has depth_cm = 3.0 (substrate.rs:28), making the default net water volume 40×25×(22−3)/1000 = 19L, not 20L. The constant 20.0 does not match the default tank's net water volume. Adding a doc comment asserting this false derivation would be actively misleading and would not catch future geometry changes — it would instead give false confidence that the constant is geometry-derived when it isn't."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"be8ec273-00b9-4ee3-8ff0-3e35a08ad0bb"}
